# BBB Server Change Discipline (Git First)

Do **not** put code, jars, configs, or test media directly onto the BBB server as a fix path.

## Required order

1. Change code in this git repo locally.
2. Commit (only when the user asks) and **push** so the remote repository is updated.
3. On the BBB server, update from that repository with the project’s approved commands (pull/checkout + install/restart as documented) — not ad-hoc `scp`/`rsync` of random files into `/usr/share/...`.

## Forbidden without explicit user request

- `scp` / `rsync` of source, jars, or patches straight into live BBB paths to “hot-fix” production
- Editing files under `/usr/share/bbb-web`, `/usr/share/bigbluebutton`, etc. by hand as the delivery method
- Dropping one-off jars (e.g. alternate `bbb-common-web-*.jar`) beside the packaged version

## Allowed

- **Read-only** SSH inspection (logs, `journalctl`, package versions, file listing) when diagnosing
- Running the **documented** deploy/update flow the user asks for (e.g. after push: server pull + package/deploy scripts)
- Local/staging workflows described in `DEPLOY-FA.md` / `.cursor/rules/bbb-deploy-pipeline.mdc` only when the user requests them — and still prefer git-backed delivery over one-off file drops

If a fix was applied out-of-band on the server, surface it and reconcile via git before considering the work done.
